# The repository routes *.csv through Git LFS for the large data-science
# datasets. This one is 955 KB and every test in this project reads it, but
# `actions/checkout` does not fetch LFS content by default -- so under LFS CI
# receives a three-line pointer file and all 29 data-backed tests fail with
# "missing column(s)", which is a confusing way to say "this is not a CSV".
#
# Un-LFS-ing it costs ~1 MB of history once. The alternative, `lfs: true` on
# the checkout, would pull every LFS object in the repository -- including the
# 127 MB bitcoin file -- into all 24 CI jobs.
data/*.csv -filter -diff -merge text
